# Currency Converter Plan

Android-only React Native + Expo + TypeScript currency viewer. **Base currency: KRW.** Shows rate cards for **USD** and **JPY** by default; **KRW** and **EUR** optional (user toggle via **표시 통화**).

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| Framework | React Native 0.86 (Expo SDK 57) |
| Language | TypeScript (strict) |
| Platform | **Android only** (`platforms: ["android"]`) |
| Build / OTA | EAS Build (`eas.json`) |
| Rates API | [Frankfurter](https://www.frankfurter.app/) — no API key |
| Calendar | `react-native-calendars` |
| Safe area | `react-native-safe-area-context` |
| Haptics | `expo-haptics` |
| Theming | `useColorScheme` + `src/theme/colors.ts` |
| Localization | `expo-localization` + `i18next` + `react-i18next` (system locale default; optional in-app override — see below) |

Bundle ID: `com.mike008.currencyconverter`

## Localization (i18n)

**Yes — use an i18n library.** With ~50 user-facing strings across screens, modals, errors, currency names, calendar labels, and date/number formatting, a small i18n setup is the right tool even without an in-app language picker. Hard-coding three languages in components does not scale and duplicates logic already split across `formatCurrency.ts`, `crossRate.ts`, and `RateDateCalendarModal.tsx`.

### Rules (current — Phase 2.5 ✅)

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Locale source (shipped) | **Android system language** — no in-app language toggle yet |
| Supported | `en`, `ko`, `ja` |
| Fallback | `en` when system locale is unsupported (e.g. `fr`, `de`) |
| Resolution | `expo-localization` `getLocales()[0].languageCode` → map `en-*` → `en`, `ko-*` → `ko`, `ja-*` → `ja` |
| Re-resolve | On `AppState` `active` so OS language changes apply after returning to the app |
| **표시 통화** modal | **Keep** — toggles optional currency cards (KRW/EUR), not UI language; shows app version at bottom (`v{semver}` from `app.json` `expo.version`, e.g. `v1.4.1`) |
| **Launcher app name** | **Fixed** `환율 변환기` (not localized; intentional) |

### Language preference — compromise (planned, not shipped)

Default **follow system**; optional **in-app override** when the user wants UI language ≠ phone language.

| Setting | Behavior |
|---------|----------|
| **System** (default) | `AsyncStorage` preference `null` / unset → use device language (current behavior) |
| **Manual** | User picks `en` \| `ko` \| `ja` in app → persist choice; ignore system until reset |
| **Reset** | “Use system language” option clears override → back to device locale |

**UI (TBD placement)** — e.g. segment or list in **표시 통화** modal, or a small **언어** entry on `HomeScreen` header. Separate from currency toggles; label clearly as language, not “표시 통화”.

**Implementation sketch**

- `src/hooks/useLanguagePreference.ts` — read/write `AsyncStorage`; expose `preference: AppLanguage \| 'system'`
- `useAppLocale` / `changeAppLanguage` — effective language = `preference === 'system' ? getDeviceLanguage() : preference`
- On `AppState` `active`: re-resolve **only when** preference is `system`
- i18n strings: `settings.languageTitle`, `settings.languageSystem`, `settings.languageEn`, etc.

**Why compromise**

- Ship simple (system-only) first — done in Phase 2.5
- Add toggle later without ripping out i18n — same `en` / `ko` / `ja` JSON files
- Covers users who keep phone in one language but want the app in another

**JS-only** → EAS Update eligible when implemented.

### Stack

```bash
npx expo install expo-localization
npm install i18next react-i18next
```

- `src/i18n/index.ts` — init `i18next`, resolve device locale, register resources
- `src/i18n/locales/en.json`, `ko.json`, `ja.json` — all UI copy
- `src/hooks/useAppLocale.ts` — BCP 47 tag for `Intl` / `toLocaleString` (`en-US`, `ko-KR`, `ja-JP`)
- Components: `useTranslation()` for labels; utils accept locale or read from i18n singleton

### String inventory (migrate from hard-coded Korean)

| Area | Examples | Notes |
|------|----------|-------|
| `HomeScreen` | 환율 변환기, 기준일, 오늘 환율, 다시 시도 | Title, hints, a11y labels |
| `CurrencySettingsModal` | 표시 통화, 닫기, hint copy, version footer | Currency toggles unchanged; version not localized |
| `RateDateCalendarModal` | 기준일 선택, 주말…, `LocaleConfig` month/day names | Per-locale calendar config |
| `crossRate.ts` | 원화, 엔화, 달러 row labels | Rename `labelKo` → `label` (i18n key or passed label) |
| `currencies.ts` | `nameKo` / `nameEn` | Replace with `t('currency.usd.name')`; drop per-locale name fields from `CurrencyConfig` |
| `formatCurrency.ts` | `ko-KR` date pattern, `formatFetchedAt` | Use `useAppLocale()` BCP 47 tag |
| `crossRate.ts` formatters | `toLocaleString('ko-KR')` | Same locale tag as formatting utils |
| Errors | `exchangeRateApi.ts`, `useExchangeRates.ts` | `t('errors.fetchFailed')`, etc. |

### Calendar locales

Register `LocaleConfig.locales.en`, `.ko`, `.ja` in `RateDateCalendarModal` (or `src/i18n/calendarLocales.ts`); set `LocaleConfig.defaultLocale` from resolved app language.

### Types / API cleanup

- `CurrencyConfig`: remove `nameKo` / `nameEn`; display name via `t(\`currency.${code.toLowerCase()}.name\`)`
- `CardConversionRow`: `labelKo` → `label`
- `getCardConversionRows`: accept `t` or return i18n keys; prefer keys in utils, translate in `CurrencyCard`

### Testing

- Android emulator: Settings → System → Languages — switch en / ko / ja and cold-start app
- Verify fallback: set system to unsupported locale → UI in English
- `npm run typecheck` after TS changes

## Display Rules

| Currency | Card label | Outputs |
|----------|------------|---------|
| USD | `$1` | 원화, 엔화 |
| JPY | `¥100` | 원화, 달러 |
| KRW | `₩1,000` | 달러, 엔화 (optional toggle) |
| EUR | `€1` | 원화 (optional toggle) |

- **Card order** — `USD` → `JPY` → `KRW` → `EUR` (`getEnabledCurrencies()`; core first, then enabled optionals in `OPTIONAL_CURRENCY_CODES` order)
- **KRW** / **EUR** — optional via **표시 통화** modal; off by default (`AsyncStorage` preference)
- API: `KRW→foreign`; invert to `krwPerUnit` (`1 / rate`)
- 교차 환율: `amount × fromKrwPerUnit / toKrwPerUnit` (`crossRate.ts`)
- **2 cards** by default (USD, JPY); up to 4 when both optionals enabled; `CARD_HEIGHT = 192`, `CARD_GAP = 12`
- Manual refresh via **오늘 환율** button only (no pull-to-refresh)

### 기준일 & Calendar

- **기준일** badge — prominent blue style; tap opens calendar modal
- Calendar opens to **selected/displayed date month** (`selectedDate ?? rates.date`)
- Selectable: weekdays only, `MIN_RATE_DATE` (1999-01-04) through today
- Disabled: weekends, TARGET/ECB holidays, future dates (`rateCalendar.ts`)
- API: `/latest` (today) or `/{YYYY-MM-DD}` (historical)
- **오늘 환율** button — always visible; calls `resetToLatest()` (fetch `/latest`, clear selected date)

### Safe Area (Android edge-to-edge)

- `edgeToEdgeEnabled=true` in `android/gradle.properties`
- `App.tsx`: `SafeAreaProvider` + `initialWindowMetrics`
- `HomeScreen`: `SafeAreaView` edges `top`, `left`, `right`, `bottom`
- `RateDateCalendarModal`: bottom `SafeAreaView` on sheet (Modal is outside parent safe area)

## Architecture

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `App.tsx` | SafeAreaProvider, StatusBar, HomeScreen entry |
| `src/types/index.ts` | `CurrencyCode` (`USD` \| `JPY` \| `EUR` \| `KRW`), `CurrencyConfig`, `ExchangeRates` |
| `src/constants/currencies.ts` | Card metadata, core/optional codes, `getEnabledCurrencies()` |
| `src/constants/appVersion.ts` | `formatAppVersion()` — `v{semver}` from `app.json` `expo.version` |
| `src/hooks/useEnabledCurrencies.ts` | Optional currency toggles + `AsyncStorage` persistence |
| `src/services/exchangeRateApi.ts` | Frankfurter fetch (`latest` or `/{date}`) + invert |
| `src/hooks/useExchangeRates.ts` | Load / refresh / selectDate / resetToLatest / needsTodayRefresh |
| `src/hooks/useLocalToday.ts` | Local date tracking (60s interval + AppState active) |
| `src/i18n/index.ts` | i18next init, device locale resolution, resource loading |
| `src/i18n/locales/{en,ko,ja}.json` | UI strings |
| `src/hooks/useAppLocale.ts` | BCP 47 locale for `Intl` / `toLocaleString` |
| `src/hooks/useLanguagePreference.ts` | *(Phase 2.5b)* `system` \| `en` \| `ko` \| `ja` override + `AsyncStorage` |
| `src/utils/formatCurrency.ts` | Currency + date formatting (locale-aware) |
| `src/utils/crossRate.ts` | USD↔JPY triangulation, foreign amount formatting |
| `src/utils/rateCalendar.ts` | Selectable dates, TARGET holidays, month marked dates |
| `src/components/CurrencyCard.tsx` | Single currency card UI |
| `src/theme/colors.ts` | Light / dark color tokens |
| `src/hooks/useAppTheme.ts` | `useColorScheme` wrapper |
| `src/components/CurrencyCardSkeleton.tsx` | Pulsing skeleton card |
| `src/components/SkeletonBone.tsx` | Animated skeleton block |
| `src/utils/haptics.ts` | Success haptic on refresh |
| `src/components/RateDateCalendarModal.tsx` | Calendar bottom sheet (en/ko/ja `LocaleConfig`, themed) |
| `src/components/CurrencySettingsModal.tsx` | **표시 통화** bottom sheet (KRW/EUR toggles + version footer) |
| `src/screens/HomeScreen.tsx` | Header, date badge, refresh banner, card stack, last-fetched time |

Keep **rate math in service/utils**, not in components.

